+			if (od->ll123_supported)
+				dma_pool_destroy(od->desc_pool);
```
(added inside the second error path after the `pr_warn` call)

Reason: Adding `dma_pool_destroy()` under the same `od->ll123_supported` condition ensures the DMA pool is properly freed before the function returns or continues cleanup, eliminating the resource leak.

